Z||000002||SPDFREK||06-01-2001||12:04 AM||||looks like some one "hard" wired the cooling fan to the fan for the heater/AC. not to sure though, can't see the fan motor. if you want to fix it, you have to see if the relay works, then have to see if the brain is turning the relay on. (that is if that red wire goes to the fan that is.)if the brain sends the volts  to the relay, and the rely is letting the voltage flow through it, then you would have bad wires if the fan is working in the current condition. remember though, I can't tell where the red wire is running. the other red wire (the one connected to the smaller wires closest to the drivers fender) I have no clue as to what it would be running to, as the cooling fan is the only Electrical thing up front cept the headlights. might want to see if they run up there. hope this helps somewhat.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by SPDFREK (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||SPDFREK||06-01-2001||12:44 AM||||Secong thought is, maybe they "hard" wired 12 volts to the fan motor for the heater/AC. if thats the case then the wires are more then likely bad. I can't really see where the red wires are running. Is the red wire one big loop? or are there 2 red ones going different places?<P>------------------<BR>'88 Fiero 4cycl Turbo,<BR>'88 Fiero GT,<BR>'72 Nova 383 stroker||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||06-01-2001||12:59 AM||||The "master electrician" that owned your Fiero owned mine at one time as well.  I found the same exact thing with mine.<P>I don't think the wires are burnt up.  What the guy tired doing was to hook up the radiator fan to the vent fan blower so he could contol the rad fan speed from inside.  The voltage wouldn't have been any different than that powering the vent blower.  I'm pretty sure the switch you found was his attempt at setting up an on/off switch on the vent blower circuit, which was stupid because you can turn off the vent blower.  The red wires, cut/disconnect those from the black and purple wires first.  Cut or disconnect the white wires and switch from the red wires as well.  Where do the red wires go?  One go to a ground, the other to the radiator fan?<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trunk_4.jpg">      <BR>The black wire plug goes on the right side of the vent/heater blower motor, the purple on the left.  You may want to check voltage between those two wires with a voltmeter first (voltage should vary as you turn the vent fan control.  No shorts, that should get the vent blower motor going again.<P>The relay for the radiator fan is ahead of the driver's side headlight.  To get a better look at the wiring you'll want to remove the headlight bucket.  It comes out by loosening the lower two 10mm nuts and removing the top two.  Take a picture of what's going on up there and the red wires and get back with the forum so we can try to help you figure this mess out.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||1
